      "side": 1,
      "message": "I assumed so. Interestingly, the action succeeds on RBE without these files and prints the same output. Only when running locally does metalava touch these files and causes the sandbox to fail the action. Metalava reads these files when looking through siblings of package html files (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:tools/metalava/src/main/java/com/android/tools/metalava/Driver.kt;l\u003d1167?q\u003dDriver.kt).\n\nAny ideas how to clean up this dependency? aurimas@ omakoto@.\nIs this code block necessary? What happens when we have the wrong package name? Would metalava fail down the line?",
      "parentUuid": "93f6278c_00748dae",
